        "is": "ps2-dvd-311"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "bios.bin",
      "display": "NAMCO System 246/256 BIOS",
      "description": "The arcade board's own boot ROM, copied from a COH-H motherboard. This is NOT a retail PlayStation 2 BIOS, and a retail one does not work: the arcade boot software differs in many module interfaces, and an arcade game does not start on it. A COH-H ROM identifies itself in its ROMVER text (region T followed by a Z). The board it came from is identified by its EXTINFO build serial, which is the only thing that tells the three boards apart. This project asks for the System 246 Rack C ROM, serial 20021119-163841, 2 MB. Redump calls the file ps2-arcade-0100tz-20021119-163841.bin. MAME has the same bytes as r27v1602f.7d in its sys246 BIOS set, and the file is also found as 246C.bin.",
