            "is": "coh-h-246c"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "bios.bin",
      "display": "NAMCO System 246/256 BIOS",
      "description": "The arcade board's own boot ROM, copied from a COH-H motherboard. This is NOT a retail PlayStation 2 BIOS, and a retail one does not work: the arcade boot software differs in many module interfaces, and an arcade game does not start on it. A COH-H ROM identifies itself in its ROMVER text (region T followed by a Z). The board it came from is identified by its EXTINFO build serial, which is the only thing that tells the three boards apart. This project asks for the System 256 ROM, serial 20040519-145634, 2 MB. Redump calls the file ps2-arcade-0100tz-20040519-145634.bin, and MAME has the same bytes as r27v1602f.8g in its sys256 BIOS set. A Super System 256 runs this same ROM with a faster bus clock, which is why both machines ask for it.",
