    {
      "id": "bios.bin",
      "display": "NAMCO System 246/256 BIOS",
      "description": "The arcade board's own boot ROM, copied from a COH-H motherboard. This is NOT a retail PlayStation 2 BIOS, and a retail one does not work: the arcade boot software differs in many module interfaces, and an arcade game does not start on it. A COH-H ROM identifies itself in its ROMVER text (region T followed by a Z). The board it came from is identified by its EXTINFO build serial, which is the only thing that tells the three boards apart. This project asks for the System 256 ROM as a 4 MB file with its two megabytes written twice. A copying tool that reads the whole address range produces this, and the file is widely found under the name 256.BIN. It describes the same System 256 machine as the 2 MB file above. The bytes are different, and this core accepts firmware only by its exact hash.",
      "size": 4194304,
