      "description": "The arcade board's own boot ROM, copied from a COH-H motherboard. This is NOT a retail PlayStation 2 BIOS, and a retail one does not work: the arcade boot software differs in many module interfaces, and an arcade game does not start on it. A COH-H ROM identifies itself in its ROMVER text (region T followed by a Z). The board it came from is identified by its EXTINFO build serial, which is the only thing that tells the three boards apart. This project asks for the ROM of the COH-H A-000-010 board, serial 20000901-114731, 4 MB, usually called COH-H31000.BIN. It is the earliest of the three and the one the arcade development boards had.",
